<!--
   QML card deck style "Stardust Dark" - the counterpart to the card back
   data/gfx/qml/backside/stardust/. The light sister variant is
   cards/stardust_light.

   A rebuild of the classic PokerTH card deck "Stardust" (Etienne Genot, 2009)
   in the QML/SVG framework. Since the themed QML decks are index/pip based (no
   illustrated court cards), the look is met through typography + colour world:
   a dark "space" card face with a blue gradient and a fine star field, a bevel
   frame in the suit colour. A four colour deck like nobus_4c_classic, adapted
   to the dark ground: diamonds=light blue, hearts=red, spades=silver white,
   clubs=green; every glyph/pip with a thin outline + drop shadow so that it
   stands out.

   The rank glyphs are paths from Orbitron (Google Fonts, OFL, see
   data-copyright.txt) - a square sci-fi typeface that comes closest to the
   Eurostile-like font used in the original. The suit paths come from the
   cards/default set, as with the other QML decks.

   The arrangement of rank index and suit symbols follows
   cards/nobus_4c_classic: rank at the top left, the small suit symbol below it,
   the large suit symbol at the bottom right - an identical layout for all
   cards, court cards included.

   Engine index -> card (see CardImage.qml):
     Suit = floor(index / 13): 0-12 diamonds(♦), 13-25 hearts(♥), 26-38 spades(♠), 39-51 clubs(♣)
     Rank = index % 13:        0=2, 1=3, … 8=10, 9=jack, 10=queen, 11=king, 12=ace

   Generated with generate_stardust_deck.py.
-->
<PokerTH>
  <CardDeck>
     <StyleDescription value="Stardust Dark (QML/SVG)" /><!-- Shown in the style selection -->
     <StyleMaintainerName value="PokerTH Development Team" />
     <StyleMaintainerEMail value="webmaster@pokerth.net" />
     <StyleCreateDate value="10.07.2026" />
     <PokerTHStyleFileVersion value="2" /><!-- Matches the version supported by the widget client -->
     <Preview value="preview.png" /><!-- Preview image (landscape only - no portrait needed) -->
     <BigIndexesActionBottom value="0" />
  </CardDeck>
</PokerTH>
